         "The convergence of big data and artificial intelligence has given rise to surveillance capitalism, where personal data is aggressively commodified. || Conglomerates harvest behavioural data to predict and manipulate consumer desires and political affiliations. This pervasive monitoring erodes personal autonomy and traps citizens inside polarizing echo chambers. Moreover, vulnerable centralized databases invite catastrophic breaches. || Safeguarding digital privacy requires stringent legislative interventions, such as universal data protection laws enforcing strict consent. Empowering individuals with data sovereignty is paramount. || Ultimately, privacy must be defended as an inviolable human right.",
