         "Artificial intelligence has achieved remarkable breakthroughs in medical imaging, frequently outperforming human physicians in diagnostic accuracy. || The integration of machine learning offers rapid analysis of complex genomic data and eliminates fatigue-related errors. However, purely algorithmic medicine risks depersonalising patient care and overlooking clinical intuition. || To preserve medical humanism, hospitals must ensure AI serves as a supportive instrument. Patients retain the absolute right to informed consent and transparent communication. || Ultimately, healing requires a harmonious synthesis of technological precision and empathetic human care.",
